[Music]  oh  [Music]  it's an early morning in may  and for 1.6 billion muslims around the  world  now is also the holy month of ramadan  marked by 30 days of fasting from  sunrise to sunset evenings are spent  together with family over a breakfast  meal called iflat  we followed five women  in five countries  as they prepare for this evening  [Music]  the day begins at 10  [Music]  my name is nancy hawk and i live in  pleasanton california  i'll be making a traditional bangladeshi  we'll have boot which is garbanzo beans  also hot petas which is meat stuffed in  puff pastry and also making some shrimp  curry because my boys love it with some  paratha  it's not hard to cook actually if i  think about it i probably cook the most  during ramadan for some reason maybe  because i'm not eating and i'm so  excited by a star  that i i want to make a lot of different  types of dishes for my family and eat  together  this excitement is echoed  kitchen to kitchen  family to family  [Music]  vacancy  [Music]  but in syria the sentiment is  [Music]  [Music]  overall there is a sense of solidarity  between the women in the kitchen amongst  the frenzy of chopping and boiling this  is their domain  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  national  [Music]  foreign  i learned to cook these dishes from my  mom my mother-in-law and my  sister-in-law each of them have their  own take of recipes that they choose  from  my sister-in-law is really good with  shortcuts my mother-in-law has a lot of  traditional recipes and my mom has the  recipes that she made when i was growing  up so i like to just pull from each of  them  as the day progresses the effects of the  fast begin to settle  [Music]  harmony  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  ascent it approaches and the time for  the call to prayer nears preparations  for the aflar come to a head raiden i  want you to put a white plate on each  mat  ramadan is not just about fasting it's  about cleansing yourself  [Music]  and so the 30 days it forces you to  reflect and think about all of that  and because everyone's doing it together  with your family or your extended family  it's a way to reinforce that and see how  can you be better  and then everything stops  around the world echoing across  landscapes is  the fourth cult of prayer of the day  [Music]  with dates and water at the ready it's  time to break their  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  ramadan is a really special month the  whole muslim community is a part of it  and it's really special to know that  we're all breaking fast together no  matter where we are it might be often  timing a little bit but this is one of  the few days where we actually sit  around the table and we eat together  which is really heartwarming  [Music]  hi my name is beryl sharachewski i  produce the ramadan around the world  series it took 10 filmmakers to bring  this project to life there are five  other stories the link is below in the  comments if you want to check them out  and over on our youtube community page  we have a q a with the filmmakers i hope  you like it

